meta {
  name: 65 Uploads
  seq: 65
}

docs {
  # Uploads

  Generic S3-backed file upload (`uploads` module). Business-authenticated; the
  tenant comes from the JWT and namespaces the S3 key. The endpoint pushes the
  file to S3 and returns only its public URL — no DB row is written. Callers
  persist that URL string into their own `attachmentUrl` field (e.g. finance
  **Receive Invoice Payment** and **Settle Settlement**).

  Endpoints:
  - `POST /uploads/attachment` — business-authenticated; upload one file
    (multipart `file`), returns `{ url }`.
  - `POST /siteadmin/uploads/attachment` — SiteAdmin-authenticated (images only);
    for global PDF-template images/watermarks. Stored under a fixed
    `global/pdf-templates` namespace (no tenant). Returns `{ url }`.

  Requires `AWS_REGION` / `AWS_BUCKET` / `AWS_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SECRET_KEY` in the
  server env; otherwise 500 `UPLOAD_NOT_CONFIGURED`. Run **Business Auth → Login**
  (business route) or **SiteAdmin Auth → Login** (siteadmin route) first so the
  matching access token is populated.
}
